# {{ profile_name }}

An OSPREY build profile, materialized from the bundled `{{ preset_name }}`
preset. Everything the preset configures is written out here explicitly —
nothing is inherited at build time, and nothing is hidden inside the OSPREY
package. This directory is yours.

## The pipeline

```
PRESET  ──materialize──>  PROFILE DIR  ──build──>  PROJECT  ──deploy──>  RUNNING
(bundled)                 (this dir)               (derived)             (containers)
```

You are at step two. The preset was a starting point; this directory is now
the source of truth. The project you build from it is a derived artifact —
regenerable, and safe to delete and rebuild at any time.

## What you own, and what OSPREY owns

**Yours — edit freely, keep in version control:**

```
{{ profile_dirname }}/
  profile.yml     the full configuration
  data/           facility content: channel databases, knowledge, lattice, scenarios
{% if persona_profiles %}  personas/       one profile per web-terminal persona, each reading ../data
{% endif %}  overlays/       your own artifacts, copied into the project at build time
    rules/                  facility rule .md files
    skills/                 custom skill directories (each with a SKILL.md)
    agents/                 custom subagent .md files
    web-terminal-context/   per-user web-terminal persona content
  README.md       this file
```

**OSPREY's — regenerated on every build, never hand-edited in the project:**
the safety hooks, the `.claude/` scaffolding, `.mcp.json` wiring, the app
templates, and the container service definitions.

## Building a project

```
osprey build <PROJECT_NAME> {{ profile_filename }}
```

Make durable changes here — in `profile.yml`, `data/`, or `overlays/` — then
rebuild. Changes made directly inside a built project are lost on the next
build.

